; DB connection config consumed by Utils\Connectivity\Database.
;
; Sections are keyed by database name (the section header IS the database
; name), and the connector resolves a database to its [<dbname>] section:
;
;   $conn = Database::connectAs($dbname, $account)
;
; $account is a service-account name owned by this repo: admin (read-write),
; reader (read), public (anonymous read). The connector reads its password
; from the <ACCOUNT>_PASSWORD key (uppercased account name + _PASSWORD); an
; empty value means a passwordless account. The keys are written by
; bin/gen-service-users (this repo's service-user provisioning) and preserved
; unchanged by gen-reuter.
;
; This file carries prod connectivity only, generated per database by
; gen-reuter from etc/machines.ini + etc/deploy.conf (one [<dbname>] section
; per mapped database — simo and analytics). The dev sandbox lives in
; var/sandbox/<name>-<guid>/reuter.ini (generated by 'ema sandbox srv/<name>-<GUID>'), not here.
;
; SERVERNAME (optional): host pin for the admin/reader accounts (default
; 'localhost'). Set it to the DB host's ZeroTier IP (or '%') here when the app
; servers reach this database over the overlay network, before running
; bin/gen-service-users. The public account is always pinned to '%'
; (anonymous, any-host read; its per-table SELECT grants live in pkg/,
; applied by ema).
;
; Transport: the section is authoritative for the 'ema' CLI. When
; MYSQL_UNIX_PORT is set, ema connects via that socket (root/unix_socket
; auth); otherwise it uses SERVER/PORT over TCP. The app layer
; (Utils\Connectivity\Database) reads MYSQL_UNIX_PORT from .env, not from
; this file, so in prod it stays TCP-only (.env is MYSQL_*-free).

[simo]
SERVER=10.147.x.10
PORT=3307
DBMS=mariadb
ADMIN_PASSWORD=
READER_PASSWORD=
PUBLIC_PASSWORD=
MYSQL_UNIX_PORT=/path/to/mysql.sock
